<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">

<reference id="supported-audio-formats">
  <title>Supported Audio Formats</title>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>audio formats<indexterm>lossless</indexterm></indexterm>
        <indexterm>audio formats<indexterm>lossy</indexterm></indexterm>
        <indexterm>export</indexterm>
        <!-- Dangling redirect: "codecs" is not itself an index entry anywhere,
             so a reader who follows "see codecs" lands nowhere. -->
        <indexterm>compression<index-see>codecs</index-see></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <refbody>
    <section>
      <p>Audacity can import and export audio in several formats.
      The table below summarizes the most commonly used formats and their characteristics.
      Lossless formats preserve the full <abbreviated-form keyref="gl-bitdepth"/> of the source.</p>
    </section>
    <table>
      <tgroup cols="4">
        <colspec colname="format" colwidth="1*"/>
        <colspec colname="type" colwidth="1*"/>
        <colspec colname="quality" colwidth="1*"/>
        <colspec colname="notes" colwidth="2*"/>
        <thead>
          <row>
            <entry>Format</entry>
            <entry>Type</entry>
            <entry>Quality</entry>
            <entry>Notes</entry>
          </row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>WAV</entry>
            <entry>Uncompressed</entry>
            <entry>Lossless</entry>
            <entry>Default format on Windows.
            Large file sizes but no quality loss.
            Best for archiving and further editing.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>MP3</entry>
            <entry>Compressed</entry>
            <entry>Lossy</entry>
            <entry>Widely supported and small file sizes.
            Good for sharing and web distribution.
            Requires the LAME encoder.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>OGG Vorbis</entry>
            <entry>Compressed</entry>
            <entry>Lossy</entry>
            <entry>Open-source alternative to MP3.
            Good quality at lower bitrates.
            Natively supported by Audacity.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>FLAC</entry>
            <entry>Compressed</entry>
            <entry>Lossless</entry>
            <entry>Smaller files than WAV with no quality loss.
            Ideal for archiving when storage space is a concern.</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </tgroup>
    </table>
  </refbody>
</reference>
